WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:03.331
Telnyx is a cloud phone provider.

00:00:03.331 --> 00:00:07.813
This video shows how the Telnyx tab connects the platform to a Telnyx

00:00:07.813 --> 00:00:11.280
account, and what you can tune once it is connected:

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:16.240
noise suppression, answering machine detection, the speaking voice, and more.

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:23.355
You give the platform a Telnyx A.P.I.

00:00:23.355 --> 00:00:23.940
key.

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:29.088
When you click Connect Telnyx, it creates the call control application, the S.I.P.

00:00:29.088 --> 00:00:34.060
connection, the outbound voice profile and the webhook on your account for you.

00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:39.250
The options below the connection appear only once you are connected.

00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:43.510
This demo site has no Telnyx account, so this video shows the tab

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:46.930
as it is before connecting, and describes the rest.

00:00:51.230 --> 00:00:56.141
Open Settings, Communication, Telephony, and choose the Telnyx tab.

00:00:56.141 --> 00:00:58.563
A short guide lists the steps:

00:00:58.563 --> 00:01:00.043
create an A.P.I.

00:01:00.043 --> 00:01:06.300
key in the Telnyx portal, save, click Connect Telnyx, and paste the webhook public key.

00:01:06.895 --> 00:01:11.388
Tick Enable Telnyx provider to make it a choice for the default provider.

00:01:11.388 --> 00:01:12.639
Paste the A.P.I.

00:01:12.639 --> 00:01:17.075
key; it is stored encrypted, and the box stays empty when you come back.

00:01:17.577 --> 00:01:21.614
The Connect Telnyx button appears once a key is stored.

00:01:21.614 --> 00:01:26.115
Here, no key is saved, so the page says to enter one and save.

00:01:26.115 --> 00:01:31.277
Connect needs a real Telnyx account, so it is not clicked in this video.

00:01:35.477 --> 00:01:40.971
After Connect, the tab shows Connected to Telnyx with the connection ids it created.

00:01:40.971 --> 00:01:46.587
Disconnect deletes those resources on Telnyx after you confirm, so you can start over.

00:01:47.337 --> 00:01:51.458
Pick the Default outbound caller id from your voice addresses.

00:01:51.458 --> 00:01:54.973
Paste the Webhook public key from the Telnyx portal.

00:01:54.973 --> 00:02:00.367
Until it is set, every call event from Telnyx is rejected and calls do not connect.

00:02:04.567 --> 00:02:08.660
Noise suppression cleans background sound out of the call audio.

00:02:08.660 --> 00:02:12.111
Choose Krisp when callers can hear colleagues nearby.

00:02:12.111 --> 00:02:17.081
Suppression strength runs from Light to Strong, and you choose whether to clean

00:02:17.081 --> 00:02:20.181
the agent's voice, the caller's voice, or both.

00:02:20.181 --> 00:02:21.467
Telnyx bills it.

00:02:22.217 --> 00:02:28.159
Answering machine detection decides whether a person or a voicemail answered an automated

00:02:28.159 --> 00:02:31.161
call, so a message is left after the tone.

00:02:31.161 --> 00:02:35.227
Premium and Standard are billed per call; Off turns it off.

00:02:35.977 --> 00:02:40.936
Text-to-speech voice and language set how phone menus, the voicemail greeting and a

00:02:40.936 --> 00:02:43.164
queue's callback offer are spoken.

00:02:43.164 --> 00:02:45.337
Leave them blank for the default.

00:02:49.537 --> 00:02:54.115
Audio test destination is a Telnyx number that echoes audio back, so the

00:02:54.115 --> 00:02:58.693
soft phone's Run audio test can check the sound without a second person.

00:02:58.693 --> 00:03:03.388
Calls with no local record chooses between reporting a call left over from

00:03:03.388 --> 00:03:05.207
a restart, and ending it.

00:03:05.957 --> 00:03:11.685
Soft phone region picks the Telnyx region the browser connects to, Credential lifetime

00:03:11.685 --> 00:03:17.600
sets how long each soft phone login lasts, and Preferred audio codecs orders the formats.

00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:22.207
Change them only when Telnyx support asks, or your network needs it.

00:03:24.207 --> 00:03:28.922
Enable Telnyx, store the key, connect, add the webhook key and a caller

00:03:28.922 --> 00:03:32.045
id, and tune the sound only when you need to.

00:03:32.045 --> 00:03:33.637
Thanks for watching.

